   "gap": "(1) Barwise p.44 claims that, by Beth's Theorem, a relation implicitly but not explicitly definable cannot occur in L_omega1omega (Beth definability for L_omega1omega). This claimed theorem has no host and no specific missing-work record: w02-p02-005.tex:1296-1304 only reports it, and def:p02-w02c-p02-003-beyond-boundary (owned body 285-319) records only the failure of Beth for weak second-order logic. Supply Beth definability for L_omega1omega with exact hypotheses and a complete proof route, or a specific missing-work record naming the missing steps. (2) Barwise p.16 claims that Goedel's Second Incompleteness Theorem tells how to find a sentence true in Z but not a consequence of a given effective list T of true axioms. Neither thm:p02-w02c-p02-003-integers (owned body 371-400, non-constructive incompleteness via Tarski) nor def:p02-w02c-p02-003-theories-boundary (owned body 402-427) nor w02-p02-005.tex:474-491 hosts or records this claim. Supply it with exact hypotheses and a proof route, or a specific missing-work record. (3) Exact hypotheses of 5.7: the general-language theorem is proved under the handbook reading def:p02-w02c-p02-003-general-reading (occurrence and replacement conditions not named in 5.7; owned body 170-180); comparison with Barwise 1974 is blocked (source not held). (4) Owned files not yet on the route.",
